{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{#
  What every page of one booking's file shares (§6.4, §6.15, issue #462):
  its title, whether the stay is under way, the booking's own rail of
  chips — and the scripts that make every form below it answer in place.

  Behind RentalAuthorizationService and reached only by a manager of THIS
  asset, which is why the pages carry what the public surfaces never do:
  the renter's identity, the internal comments, the full history.

  **The booking's rail replaces the asset's.** Stacking the two would be two
  rows of chips answering two different questions; a « back to the asset »
  chip would be a third. The breadcrumb already goes back — the controller
  hands it the asset and its bookings list as real links
  (`breadcrumb_trail`) — so this page shows one rail, and it is the
  booking's.

  **Every page is refreshable in place.** public/assets/js/rental-booking.js
  posts a page's forms with fetch and replaces the contents of each
  `data-booking-panel` wrapper from a fresh render of the SAME URL, so a
  page only ever swaps the panels it renders. `data-rental-booking` is on
  the frame for that reason: every page opts in by existing.

  Requires `booking`, `asset`, `booking_page` (a Booking\BookingPage),
  `booking_pages` (the pages offered on this booking) and `booking_url`.
#}
{% block title %}{{ booking.reference }}{% if booking_page.value != 'dashboard' %} — {{ booking_page.label }}{% endif %} — {{ asset.name }} — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
    <div class="page-medium" data-rental-booking data-booking-page="{{ booking_page.value }}">
        {% include 'partials/page_header.html.twig' with {
            title: booking.reference,
            subtitle: booking.renterName ~ ' · du ' ~ booking.arrivalDate|date_fr ~ ' au ' ~ booking.departureDate|date_fr,
        } only %}
        <div data-booking-panel="in-progress">
            {% if is_in_progress %}
                <p class="mb-3">{% include 'partials/status_badge.html.twig' with { status: 'active', label: 'En cours' } only %}</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {% include '@rental/management/_booking_nav.html.twig' %}

        {% block booking_content %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
    {# Turns every form on the page into a fetch, then re-renders the panels. #}
    <script src="{{ asset('/assets/js/rental-booking.js') }}" defer></script>
    {# Opens the box a fragment names — a journey line on the dashboard
       pointing into another page, and any link sent from elsewhere. #}
    <script src="{{ asset('/assets/js/collapse-anchor.js') }}" defer></script>
    {% block booking_scripts %}{% endblock %}
{% endblock %}
